{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01XbE54DmboWYiLdsWtJhgD3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can't easily check the openssl API directly. Let me try a different approach to fix the `set_root_certificates` function.\n\nThe issues are:\n1. `openssl::foreign_types` module doesn't exist (or isn't public)\n2. `X509Store::as_ptr()` and `X509::as_ptr()` are not accessible without a trait\n\nI have several options:\n1. Use `X509StoreRef::add_cert` which should be available in openssl 0.10.79 \n2. Add the `foreign-types` crate as a direct dependency\n\n\n3. Use a completely different approach\n\nFor option 1, I'm thinking `X509StoreRef::add_cert` should work since `X509Store` dereferences to `X509StoreRef` automatically, and this method has been stable in openssl for a while. Let me check if that resolves the issue.\n\nActually, the real problems were the FFI imports and trying to call `as_ptr` on types that don't expose it. If I switch to using the safe `X509StoreRef::add_cert` method instead of raw FFI calls, I can avoid those errors entirely. I'm rewriting the function to parse certificates from DER format and add them to the store using the high-level API.\n\nRewriting the implementation... I'm working through the auto-deref chain in Rust—when calling `self.store.add_cert(cert)` on a mutable reference, it should properly resolve to `X509StoreRef::add_cert` which takes `&self` due to OpenSSL's internal mutability. Now I need to clean up the imports by removing `openssl_sys` and `ForeignType`, and decide whether to keep the `openssl-sys` dependency in Cargo.toml or remove it entirely since it's no longer being used.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":177,"cache_read_input_tokens":160723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":177},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce9760c1-0503-4891-9073-2bbfbb3810ec","uuid":"cd1a4f19-7c06-4112-863f-84f3a107784c"}
