{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016uw3fXeqy6Jkv48K4PZFsJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1536\t/// strings.  C: `get_certs_from_file` (which allocated both the\n1537\t/// outer iovec array and each `base` slot — the Rust shape owns\n1538\t/// both via the nested `Vec<Vec<u8>>`).  Returns `None` when the\n1539\t/// loader callback is unset or the file fails to parse.\n1540\tpub fn get_certs_from_file(file_name: &str) -> Option<Vec<Vec<u8>>> {\n1541\t    let contents = std::fs::read_to_string(file_name).ok()?;\n1542\t    let begin = \"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\";\n1543\t    let end = \"-----END CERTIFICATE-----\";\n1544\t    let mut certs = Vec::new();\n1545\t    let mut rest = contents.as_str();\n1546\t    while let Some(start) = rest.find(begin) {\n1547\t        let after_begin = &rest[start + begin.len()..];\n1548\t        let stop = after_begin.find(end)?;\n1549\t        let b64 = &after_begin[..stop];\n1550\t        certs.push(base64_decode_clean(b64)?);\n1551\t        rest = &after_begin[stop + end.len()..];\n1552\t    }\n1553\t    if certs.is_empty() { None } else { Some(certs) }\n1554\t}\n1555\t\n1556\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1557\t// Retry-packet integrity protection.\n1558\t//\n1559\t// These manage a small set of AEAD contexts (one per supported\n1560\t// QUIC version) used to compute retry-packet integrity tags.\n1561\t\n1562\t/// Build a retry-protection AEAD context from the retry integrity\n1563\t/// key for a given version.  C: `create_retry_protection_context`.\n1564\tpub fn create_retry_protection_context(\n1565\t    is_enc: bool,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HUvr9rnNYfbmjJkXiGVZwB","session_id":"ce9760c1-0503-4891-9073-2bbfbb3810ec","uuid":"75902ec9-4bae-4853-aa61-3901b9030e69","timestamp":"2026-05-07T08:05:52.665Z"}
