{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a \"Phase 4B missing implementation batch\" requiring faithful translation of 5 C functions to Rust with strict rules: no `todo!()`, no `unimplemented!()`, no placeholder returns, no stubs. The 5 items were:\n   - `ech_opener_callback` (C: `picoquic/ech.c:230-267`) → `EchOpenerState::open` in `rs/fq/src/ech.rs` — had a `todo!()` for HPKE DHKEM decapsulation\n   - `picoquic_ech_get_retry_config` (C: `picoquic/ech.c:1067-1075`) → `Connection::ech_retry_config` in `rs/fq/src/lib.rs` — marked as containing incomplete markers\n   - `picoquic_openssl_set_tls_root_certificates` (C: `picoquic/picoquic_ptls_openssl.c:298-319`) → `rs/fq/src/sys/openssl.rs` — no Rust counterpart existed\n   - `set_openssl_sign_certificate_from_key` (C: `picoquic/picoquic_ptls_openssl.c:110-136`) → `rs/fq/src/sys/openssl.rs` — no Rust counterpart existed\n   - `cmsg_format_header_return_data_ptr` (C: `picoquic/picosocks.c:519-543`) → `rs/fq/src/socks.rs` — no Rust counterpart existed\n\n   Verification gates specified: `cargo fmt`, `cargo test --no-run`, `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - HPKE (RFC 9180) — Hybrid Public Key Encryption, `hpke` crate v0.12, base-mode receiver setup (`SetupBaseR`), DHKEM(X25519/P-256/P-384), `Context.Export`\n   - picotls OpenSSL backend — `ptls_openssl_sign_certificate_t`, `ptls_hpke_setup_base_r`, `ptls_context_t`\n   - OpenSSL Rust bindings — `openssl` crate v0.10.79, `X509Store`, `X509StoreBuilder`, `X509StoreRef`, `X509StoreRef::add_cert`\n   - `foreign-types` crate v0.3.2 — `ForeignType` trait providing `as_ptr()` on OpenSSL wrapper types\n   - Unix control messages — `struct msghdr`, `struct cmsghdr`, `CMSG_FIRSTHDR`, `CMSG_NXTHDR`, `CMSG_SPACE`, `CMSG_LEN`, `CMSG_DATA`\n   - `libc` crate v0.2 — for Unix-specific socket ancillary data types\n   - Rust 2024 edition — `unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn`: unsafe operations inside `unsafe fn` require explicit `unsafe {}` blocks\n   - c2rust branch translation project — translating picoquic C library to safe idiomatic Rust in `rs/fq/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`rs/fq/Cargo.toml`** — Dependencies file. Added `hpke = { version = \"0.12\", features = [\"x25519\", \"p256\", \"p384\"] }` and `libc = \"0.2\"`. The `openssl-sys` optional dep was added then removed (two cycles). Final state:\n     ```toml\n     hpke = { version = \"0.12\", features = [\"x25519\", \"p256\", \"p384\"] }\n     libc = \"0.2\"\n     openssl = { version = \"0.10\", optional = true }\n     [features]\n     sys-openssl = [\"dep:openssl\"]\n     ```\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/ech.rs`** — ECH helpers module. Multiple changes:\n     - Module-level doc comment updated (removed \"currently `todo!()`\" language)\n     - `EchOpenResult` doc comment updated (removed \"Empty until the DHKEM decapsulation is implemented\")\n     - `EchOpenerState::open` doc comment: removed `# Blocker` section\n     - `EchOpenerState::open` body: replaced `todo!()` block with:\n       ```rust\n       let key_material =\n           hpke_setup_receiver(self.kem_id, cipher, &self.private_key, enc, &info)?;\n       Some(EchOpenResult { cipher, key_material })\n       ```\n     - Added private `hpke_setup_receiver` function after `EchOpenerState` impl:\n       ```rust\n       fn hpke_setup_receiver(\n           kem: u16,\n           cipher: HpkeCipherSuiteId,\n           private_key: &[u8],\n           enc: &[u8],\n           info: &[u8],\n       ) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n           use hpke::{Deserializable, Kem as HpkeKem, OpModeR};\n           macro_rules! run_hpke {\n               ($KemType:ty, $KdfType:ty, $AeadType:ty) => {{\n                   let sk = <$KemType as HpkeKem>::PrivateKey::from_bytes(private_key).ok()?;\n                   let ek = <$KemType as HpkeKem>::EncappedKey::from_bytes(enc).ok()?;\n                   let ctx = hpke::setup_receiver::<$AeadType, $KdfType, $KemType>(\n                       &OpModeR::Base, &sk, &ek, info,\n                   ).ok()?;\n                   let mut out = alloc::vec![0u8; 32];\n                   ctx.export(b\"picoquic ech key material\", &mut out).ok()?;\n                   Some(out)\n               }};\n           }\n           match (kem, cipher.kdf, cipher.aead) {\n               (kem_id::X25519_SHA256, kdf_id::HKDF_SHA256, aead_id::AES_128_GCM) => {\n                   run_hpke!(hpke::kem::X25519HkdfSha256, hpke::kdf::HkdfSha256, hpke::aead::AesGcm128)\n               }\n               (kem_id::X25519_SHA256, kdf_id::HKDF_SHA256, aead_id::CHACHA20_POLY1305) => {\n                   run_hpke!(hpke::kem::X25519HkdfSha256, hpke::kdf::HkdfSha256, hpke::aead::ChaCha20Poly1305)\n               }\n               (kem_id::P256_SHA256, kdf_id::HKDF_SHA256, aead_id::AES_128_GCM) => {\n                   run_hpke!(hpke::kem::DhP256HkdfSha256, hpke::kdf::HkdfSha256, hpke::aead::AesGcm128)\n               }\n               (kem_id::P384_SHA384, kdf_id::HKDF_SHA384, aead_id::AES_256_GCM) => {\n                   run_hpke!(hpke::kem::DhP384HkdfSha384, hpke::kdf::HkdfSha384, hpke::aead::AesGcm256)\n               }\n               _ => None,\n           }\n       }\n       ```\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/lib.rs`** — Item 2 (`picoquic_ech_get_retry_config`) was already correctly implemented at lines 3491-3494:\n     ```rust\n     /// C: `picoquic_ech_get_retry_config`\n     pub fn ech_retry_config(&self) -> &[u8] {\n         self.tls_ctx.as_ref().map_or(&[], |s| s.retry_configs())\n     }\n     ```\n     No changes needed.\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/sys/openssl.rs`** — Added three new items at the end:\n     1. `impl CertificateVerifier { set_root_certificates }` method — currently broken (see errors), last state:\n        ```rust\n        pub fn set_root_certificates(&mut self, certs: &[&[u8]]) -> Result<(), crate::Error> {\n            for &cert_der in certs {\n                let cert = openssl::x509::X509::from_der(cert_der)\n                    .map_err(|_| crate::Error::Generic)?;\n                self.store\n                    .add_cert(cert)\n                    .map_err(|_| crate::Error::Generic)?;\n                self.is_cert_store_not_empty = true;\n            }\n            Ok(())\n        }\n        ```\n     2. `SignCertificate` struct:\n        ```rust\n        pub struct SignCertificate {\n            pub key: openssl::pkey::PKey<openssl::pkey::Private>,\n        }\n        ```\n     3. `set_sign_certificate_from_key` private function:\n        ```rust\n        pub(crate) fn set_sign_certificate_from_key(\n            key: Option<openssl::pkey::PKey<openssl::pkey::Private>>,\n        ) -> Result<SignCertificate, crate::Error> {\n            let key = key.ok_or(crate::Error::Generic)?;\n            Ok(SignCertificate { key })\n        }\n        ```\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/socks.rs`** — Added `#[cfg(unix)] use libc;` import and `cmsg_format_header_return_data_ptr` function:\n     ```rust\n     #[cfg(unix)]\n     #[allow(dead_code)]\n     pub(crate) unsafe fn cmsg_format_header_return_data_ptr(\n         msg: *mut libc::msghdr,\n         last_cmsg: &mut *mut libc::cmsghdr,\n         control_length: &mut libc::c_int,\n         cmsg_level: libc::c_int,\n         cmsg_type: libc::c_int,\n         cmsg_data_len: usize,\n     ) -> *mut core::ffi::c_void {\n         let cmsg: *mut libc::cmsghdr = unsafe {\n             if (*last_cmsg).is_null() {\n                 libc::CMSG_FIRSTHDR(msg as *const libc::msghdr)\n             } else {\n                 libc::CMSG_NXTHDR(\n                     msg as *const libc::msghdr,\n                     *last_cmsg as *const libc::cmsghdr,\n                 )\n             }\n         };\n         if cmsg.is_null() {\n             return core::ptr::null_mut();\n         }\n         unsafe {\n             let cmsg_required_space = libc::CMSG_SPACE(cmsg_data_len as libc::c_uint) as usize;\n             *control_length += cmsg_required_space as libc::c_int;\n             core::ptr::write_bytes(cmsg as *mut u8, 0, cmsg_required_space);\n             (*cmsg).cmsg_level = cmsg_level;\n             (*cmsg).cmsg_type = cmsg_type;\n             (*cmsg).cmsg_len = libc::CMSG_LEN(cmsg_data_len as libc::c_uint) as _;\n             *last_cmsg = cmsg;\n             libc::CMSG_DATA(cmsg) as *mut core::ffi::c_void\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`/Users/richbarn/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/openssl-0.10.79/src/x509/store.rs`** — Read to understand available API. Key finding: the file uses `foreign_types::{ForeignType, ForeignTypeRef}` directly (NOT re-exported as `openssl::foreign_types`). `X509StoreBuilder` wraps `ffi::X509_STORE` via `foreign_type_and_impl_send_sync!` macro. `builder.add_cert(certificate)` is shown in the doctest but is on `X509StoreBuilder` — NOT on the built `X509Store`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n\n   - **Error: E0133 (unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn) warnings → clippy errors**\n     In `socks.rs`, the `unsafe fn cmsg_format_header_return_data_ptr` body made unsafe calls (`libc::CMSG_FIRSTHDR`, raw pointer deref, etc.) without explicit `unsafe {}` blocks. Rust 2024 edition requires these even inside `unsafe fn`.\n     - Fix: Wrapped the two unsafe regions in explicit `unsafe { ... }` blocks inside the function body.\n\n   - **Error: `openssl::foreign_types` not found + `as_ptr` not found**\n     First attempt at `set_root_certificates` used:\n     ```rust\n     use openssl::foreign_types::ForeignType;\n     openssl_sys::X509_STORE_add_cert(self.store.as_ptr(), cert.as_ptr())\n     ```\n     Failed with `error[E0432]: unresolved import 'openssl::foreign_types'` and `error[E0599]: no method named 'as_ptr'`.\n     - Fix attempt: Removed `openssl-sys` dep, removed `ForeignType` import, rewrote to use `self.store.add_cert(cert)` assuming `X509StoreRef::add_cert` exists.\n\n   - **Error (current/unresolved): `add_cert` not found on `X509Store`**\n     `error[E0599]: no method named 'add_cert' found for struct 'openssl::x509::store::X509Store'`\n     The `add_cert` method exists on `X509StoreBuilder`, NOT on the built `X509Store` or `X509StoreRef` (in openssl 0.10.79).\n     - Status: Being actively investigated. The openssl 0.10.79 store.rs source file was being read to determine the correct API when the summary was requested. The file reveals `foreign_types::{ForeignType, ForeignTypeRef}` is used directly and `add_cert` is on the builder only.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Items 1 (ech.rs), 2 (lib.rs already done), 4 (SignCertificate/set_sign_certificate_from_key in openssl.rs), and 5 (cmsg helper in socks.rs) are all compiled and pass `cargo test --no-run`.\n   - Item 3 (`set_root_certificates` in openssl.rs) still has a compile error because `X509StoreRef::add_cert` doesn't exist in openssl 0.10.79. The correct fix needs to either:\n     - Add `foreign-types = \"0.3\"` (optionally gated on `sys-openssl`) to get `ForeignType` trait and access `as_ptr()`, then use `openssl_sys::X509_STORE_add_cert` directly with raw pointers\n     - OR redesign `CertificateVerifier` to store state that allows mutation (e.g., keep the builder separate, or rebuild on demand)\n   - The openssl 0.10.79 store.rs confirms `foreign_types::{ForeignType, ForeignTypeRef}` is imported directly from the `foreign-types` crate. Adding `foreign-types = \"0.3\"` as a direct dep and using `use foreign_types::ForeignType;` would enable calling `store.as_ptr()` and `cert.as_ptr()`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single user message was the detailed Phase 4B task specification containing: the rules (\"NO SHORTCUTS\"), the forbidden patterns (`todo!()`, `unimplemented!()`, `// SKIP:`, placeholder returns), the concrete mappings for common patterns (pthread → thread::spawn, etc.), implementation rules, verification commands (`cargo test --no-run`, `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`), and the 5 specific items with their C sources, Rust destinations, and reasons.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix the remaining compile error in `sys/openssl.rs`: `set_root_certificates` fails because `X509StoreRef::add_cert` doesn't exist on openssl 0.10.79. The fix is to add `foreign-types = \"0.3\"` (under `sys-openssl` feature) and use raw FFI via `openssl_sys::X509_STORE_add_cert` with pointers obtained via `ForeignType::as_ptr()`.\n   - Run `cargo clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings` successfully after fixing the openssl issue.\n   - Run `cargo fmt` final pass.\n   - Log commands to `COMMANDS.log`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The work immediately before the summary was investigating why `self.store.add_cert(cert)` fails in `rs/fq/src/sys/openssl.rs`. The investigation involved:\n   1. Checking the installed openssl version: v0.10.79\n   2. Checking foreign-types version in Cargo.lock: v0.3.2\n   3. Reading the actual openssl 0.10.79 source at `/Users/richbarn/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/openssl-0.10.79/src/x509/store.rs`\n\n   The last read of store.rs (lines 1-80) showed:\n   - `use foreign_types::{ForeignType, ForeignTypeRef};` — the crate uses `foreign-types` directly, does NOT re-export as `openssl::foreign_types`\n   - `foreign_type_and_impl_send_sync!` macro creates `X509StoreBuilder` wrapping `ffi::X509_STORE`\n   - `add_cert` is on `X509StoreBuilder` (the builder), NOT on the built `X509Store`\n\n   Current broken code in `sys/openssl.rs`:\n   ```rust\n   pub fn set_root_certificates(&mut self, certs: &[&[u8]]) -> Result<(), crate::Error> {\n       for &cert_der in certs {\n           let cert = openssl::x509::X509::from_der(cert_der)\n               .map_err(|_| crate::Error::Generic)?;\n           self.store\n               .add_cert(cert)  // ERROR: method not found on X509Store\n               .map_err(|_| crate::Error::Generic)?;\n           self.is_cert_store_not_empty = true;\n       }\n       Ok(())\n   }\n   ```\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Fix the `set_root_certificates` compile error. The correct approach based on the openssl 0.10.79 source:\n\n   Add `foreign-types` as a direct optional dependency in Cargo.toml:\n   ```toml\n   foreign-types = { version = \"0.3\", optional = true }\n   [features]\n   sys-openssl = [\"dep:openssl\", \"dep:foreign-types\"]\n   ```\n\n   And also restore `openssl-sys` gated on the feature:\n   ```toml\n   openssl-sys = { version = \"0.9\", optional = true }\n   sys-openssl = [\"dep:openssl\", \"dep:openssl-sys\", \"dep:foreign-types\"]\n   ```\n\n   Then rewrite `set_root_certificates` to use raw FFI:\n   ```rust\n   pub fn set_root_certificates(&mut self, certs: &[&[u8]]) -> Result<(), crate::Error> {\n       use foreign_types::ForeignType;\n       for &cert_der in certs {\n           let cert = openssl::x509::X509::from_der(cert_der)\n               .map_err(|_| crate::Error::Generic)?;\n           let ret = unsafe {\n               openssl_sys::X509_STORE_add_cert(self.store.as_ptr(), cert.as_ptr())\n           };\n           if ret == 0 {\n               return Err(crate::Error::Generic);\n           }\n           self.is_cert_store_not_empty = true;\n       }\n       Ok(())\n   }\n   ```\n\n   This was the exact problem being diagnosed: the read of `openssl-0.10.79/src/x509/store.rs` revealed that `foreign_types` is imported directly in the openssl crate but not re-exported, and `add_cert` only exists on the builder, not on the built store. The fix requires `foreign-types` as a direct dep and `openssl-sys` for the raw FFI call.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/richbarn/.claude/projects/-Users-richbarn-Projects-picoquic/ce9760c1-0503-4891-9073-2bbfbb3810ec.jsonl\nContinue the conv